Add support for Hydra coordSys feature with *orthographic* projection cameras

Ortho variant of test_13221: the projector cameras are orthographic, exercising
the .camera / .NDC / .raster / .screen spaces through Arnold ortho_camera nodes.

Each grid's colour ramp window is matched to the space it projects: -5..5 for
.camera (world units), 0..1 for .NDC, -1..1 for .screen and 0..160/0..120 for
.raster. A single window cannot suit all four - with -5..5 everywhere the .NDC
grid collapsed to a flat patch and .raster was almost entirely clipped, so
neither could show a wrong projection.

.raster is in resolution-dependent units, so its window (and therefore the
expected image for that grid) is tied to the testsuite's 160x120. Rendering this
scene at another resolution legitimately changes that grid - and only that grid;
the other three spaces are resolution-independent.

See #32 / ARNOLD-13221

author: cyril.pichard

PARAMS: {'scene':'test.usda', 'kick_params':'-c /Cameras/renderCamera'}
